# An ignoring RECONSIDER while the lock is held clears the target's conflict mark and keeps the
# mark of a disconnected main block with its data (validation.cpp:4190). Spork 19 off and on
# resets the lock (chainlock/handler.cpp:209-222), and that mark outlives it: the held block on
# it is bad-prevblk-chainlock (validation.cpp:4654). The header-only child keeps that block off
# getchaintips' tips.
extend main 2
fork 0 1 headers hold
fork 0 1 hold
fork 2 2
cl tip#2
invalidate built#0
reconsider built#0 ignore_cl
spork off
cl tip#2
spork on
cl tip#2
deliver b2
